---
import { policyDates } from '../data/legal';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import ContentPage from '../layouts/ContentPage.astro';
---

<ContentPage
  title="About InsureFacts"
  description="InsureFacts is an independent website that explains how insurance works in the US, UK, Canada and Australia, using official sources. We don't sell insurance."
  lead="An independent, free guide to how insurance works in four countries, built on official sources."
  updated={policyDates.about}
  searchable
>
  <h2>Who runs InsureFacts</h2>
  <p>
    InsureFacts is an independent website run by {site.ownerName}, based in {site.ownerLocation}.
    You can contact us at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Our mission</h2>
  <p>
    Insurance is full of unfamiliar terms, and the rules differ from one country to the next. Our
    mission is to explain, in plain English, how insurance actually works in the United States, the
    United Kingdom, Canada and Australia, so that readers can understand their options and know
    where to find the official rules.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do, and what we don’t</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      We explain facts, rules and how things work, using official government and regulator sources.
    </li>
    <li>We link to every source we use, so you can check it yourself.</li>
    <li>We use each country’s own terms and spelling.</li>
    <li>
      We <strong>don’t</strong> sell insurance, compare prices, or recommend any insurer, policy or
      product.
    </li>
    <li>
      We <strong>don’t</strong> give financial advice, personal or general. Nothing on this site
      takes your circumstances into account.
    </li>
    <li>
      We are <strong>not</strong> an insurance company, agent or broker, and we don’t collect
      personal details: there are no accounts, sign-ups or forms.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our independence</h2>
  <p>
    InsureFacts is not owned by, paid by or affiliated with any insurer, broker, agent or comparison
    website. We don’t earn commission, and we don’t accept payment to mention or link to any
    company.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is free to read and is funded by advertising served by Google AdSense. Advertisers have
    no say in what we write, ads are always labelled “Advertisement”, and an ad appearing on the
    site is not an endorsement.
  </p>

  <h2>How we research and update articles</h2>
  <p>
    Our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> explains how we choose sources, check
    facts and keep articles up to date. If you spot something that’s wrong or out of date, please
    tell us: our <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a> explains how.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
